      "created_at": "2025-10-20T12:07:06.968Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I’m trying to make a <strong>child table in ERPNext read-only</strong>, so users can’t edit the field values — but I still want them to <strong>select and delete rows</strong>. However, setting the table as read-only currently disables <strong>all interaction</strong>, including row selection and deletion. I’ve tried using both “Read Only” in Customize Form and <code>frm.set_df_property('table_field', 'read_only', 1)</code> in a script, but both block any action. I’m looking for a way (or workaround) to make the <strong>rows non-editable</strong> while <strong>keeping delete and selection enabled</strong>.</p>",
